course: dictionary
lesson: 941
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word block can be a toy, a building, a rule for stopping something, or a move in sport. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it. «A tree blocked the road» tells you block means to stop something getting past.
explain: «Fish fingers are usually white fish cut into blocks» is about food, not toys. A block here is a chunk or a solid piece. Always ask: what meaning fits this sentence? Then test it by putting your meaning in place of the word and checking that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Block also appears in phrases. «Building blocks» are the toys children stack, and «a block of flats» is a large building. «Around the block» means going the long way round a row of houses. When a word is in a phrase, the whole phrase often tells you the meaning.
fact: A block can be a solid piece of wood, plastic or stone, often shaped like a cube.
fact: A block can also be a group of buildings between streets, or one big building such as «a block of flats».
fact: To block means to stop something from passing: «A tree blocked the road.»
fact: In sport, a block stops the ball or a player.
fact: «Opaque» materials block light, so no light gets through them.
fact: Long ago, the Chinese printed books with carved wooden blocks; the Diamond Sutra of 868 is the oldest dated printed book.
exercise: «A tree blocked the road.» What does blocked mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Built a tall tower | *Stopped something from getting past | Counted it carefully
exercise: Ella stacked the red block on the blue one. What is a block here? | A player who stops the ball | *A solid toy cube you can build with | A group of flats on a street | A card the bank freezes
exercise: «She lives in a block of flats near the park.» What does block mean here? | A solid cube of wood | A block in a football match | *A large building | To stop something passing
test: «Transparent materials let light through, translucent ones let some through, and opaque ones block it.» What does block mean in this sentence? | Build a tower | Hit a ball | *Stop the light from getting through | Freeze the money
test: «If a card is lost, the bank can block it at once.» What does the bank do? | Gives the card a new colour | Sends the card to school | Lets the card go faster | *Stops the card from being used
exam: Which meaning of block is used in «The Chinese printed books with carved wooden blocks»? | A stop in sport | A group of buildings between streets | To stop something from passing | *A solid piece of wood, often a cube
